 "why": "Hund's first rule across the 4D table's f block (elements 85–110, 4f⁵ to 4f³¹). The sandbox survey found it broken for every d² and d¹⁶ (26, 39, 54, 66) and for 4f³ (83, spin ½ 0.15 eV below the quartet). It holds for d³–d¹⁵, d¹⁷, 4f² and 4f⁴. The f fillings from f⁵ on have M_S blocks of 10⁴–10⁶ determinants. Each element here runs its own matrix-free Lanczos per block up to 250 000 determinants, four elements to a runner. Bigger blocks are skipped and named, so for mid-shell f the answer is a bound (no lower term among the spins run).",
